WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:21.097
stared at Zira, thinking about what Mellis had just said about not trusting her.

2
00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:23.898
"Er, nothing," she said.

3
00:00:24.378 --> 00:00:27.499
But Vilkor rushed over to Zira, clutching the purple fruit.

4
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.640
"Look!" he cried.

5
00:00:30.328 --> 00:00:31.829
"Everything is growing!

6
00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:35.029
And it's all because of my new well!"

7
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.791
Zann leaned closer to Perda.

8
00:00:40.511 --> 00:00:43.372
"So much for keeping everything a secret," he whispered.

9
00:00:43.392 --> 00:00:46.053
"I guess Vilkor is too excited to stay quiet."

10
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:50.454
Perda nodded, though she was only half listening to Zann.

11
00:00:50.894 --> 00:00:52.374
She was still watching Zira.

12
00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:57.536
The woman listened to Vilkor's babbled explanation and then looked around.

13
00:00:58.316 --> 00:01:00.717
Perda saw something in her gaze change.

14
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:04.218
"There's something about her eyes," Perda thought.

15
00:01:04.238 --> 00:01:08.139
"They look suspicious, like she's plotting something."

16
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:14.621
"I see," Zira said, her voice suddenly less confused and more amiable.

17
00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:18.722
"Congratulations on your good fortune, dear friend."

18
00:01:19.342 --> 00:01:20.783
She patted Vilkor's arm.

19
00:01:20.803 --> 00:01:27.618
"Perhaps if you show me this magical well, I can help you protect it from the greed of

20
00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:30.280
others." "Thanks, Zira."

21
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.961
Vilkor grinned at her.

22
00:01:31.981 --> 00:01:34.803
"You've always been a true friend to me.

23
00:01:35.543 --> 00:01:39.786
That's no surprise, as the two of us are clearly the smartest people in the village.

24
00:01:40.927 --> 00:01:42.368
Here—have a new hat."

25
00:01:43.028 --> 00:01:44.329
He rubbed his hands together.

26
00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.471
A moment later another fancy hat appeared.

27
00:01:48.112 --> 00:01:51.274
Zira stared at it and then glanced at Vilkor's hands.

28
00:01:51.714 --> 00:01:53.716
Perda could see what the woman was thinking.

29
00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:58.433
She was noting exactly what Vilkor had done to make the hat appear.

30
00:01:58.453 --> 00:02:01.974
"Thank you, Vilkor," Zira said.

31
00:02:01.994 --> 00:02:04.715
"Now, shall we visit your well?"

32
00:02:05.515 --> 00:02:07.616
Zann leaned closer to Perda again.

33
00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:10.377
"Let's go with them," he whispered eagerly.

34
00:02:10.397 --> 00:02:14.878
"Now that there's all this magic energy around, I bet we can open the wormhole and go home."

35
00:02:14.898 --> 00:02:16.619
"I suppose you're right."

36
00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:21.140
Perda couldn't shake the idea that Zira might be planning trouble.

37
00:02:21.896 --> 00:02:24.118
"Mellis said she didn't trust Zira though.

38
00:02:24.718 --> 00:02:26.740
What if she tries something sneaky?"

39
00:02:28.161 --> 00:02:28.961
Zann shrugged.

40
00:02:29.622 --> 00:02:30.162
"Like what?

41
00:02:30.582 --> 00:02:33.404
Now that magic is spreading in this world, nobody can control it."

42
00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:36.206
"I guess that's true," Perda said.

43
00:02:36.226 --> 00:02:40.549
"Maybe we should give Mellis a few more magic lessons before we leave though."

44
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.431
"Sure," Zann said.

45
00:02:42.451 --> 00:02:43.691
"But let's make it quick.

46
00:02:44.212 --> 00:02:48.034
We've already been missing for more than a day, and I'm sure our families and friends are worried."

47
00:02:49.275 --> 00:02:49.936
Perda nodded.

48
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.883
She wondered how long it had taken Darb and Gliss to rush back to the lab and tell

49
00:02:55.103 --> 00:02:58.165
everyone about the weird new wormhole in Wormwood.

50
00:02:58.686 --> 00:03:02.708
Would Nax and Asta try to come through it to rescue her and Zann?

51
00:03:03.589 --> 00:03:07.391
She pushed aside those thoughts as she realized Vilkor was pointing at them.

52
00:03:07.892 --> 00:03:12.735
He was telling Zira how they'd arrived suddenly at the farmhouse, seemingly out of thin air.

53
00:03:12.755 --> 00:03:15.137
"You did that with magic, right?"

54
00:03:15.517 --> 00:03:16.177
Vilkor said.

55
00:03:16.197 --> 00:03:19.900
"Perhaps that magic would save us from needing to walk all the way to the well?"

56
00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.561
"Sure," Zann said.

57
00:03:21.581 --> 00:03:23.041
"We can zap there immediately."

58
00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:26.543
Perda could tell he was about to explain how to do it.

59
00:03:26.563 --> 00:03:30.164
"Join hands," she said before he could say anything else.

60
00:03:30.184 --> 00:03:33.646
"Zann and I will transport everyone to the well."

61
00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:37.807
Zira looked curious, and Vilkor looked a little nervous.

62
00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:42.069
But they did as Perda said.

63
00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:48.412
Soon all five of them were holding hands in a line, with Zann and Perda at either end.

64
00:03:49.404 --> 00:03:52.126
Zann held onto Zing's tail with his free hand.

65
00:03:52.146 --> 00:03:54.268
"Ready?" Perda said.

66
00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.130
She rubbed her free hand against her side.

67
00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:05.155
"Zap!" When they landed, the adults immediately started babbling about the Zap.

68
00:04:06.036 --> 00:04:07.277
But Perda barely heard them.

69
00:04:07.957 --> 00:04:09.638
The place looked so different!

70
00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:12.941
There were more shrubs and trees now.

71
00:04:14.202 --> 00:04:17.184
And the original tree wasn't a scraggly sapling anymore.

72
00:04:17.992 --> 00:04:22.774
It had grown into a strong, medium-size tree, large enough to shade the well.

73
00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.736
The well itself was now filled with sparkling, rainbow-colored water.

74
00:04:27.756 --> 00:04:29.677
"Is that water?"

75
00:04:30.097 --> 00:04:30.877
Vilkor asked.

76
00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:32.738
"It looks strange!"

77
00:04:33.638 --> 00:04:37.840
Perda saw that he was still clutching the pottery cup he'd created earlier.

78
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.401
"Scoop some out," she said.

79
00:04:40.921 --> 00:04:43.282
She was a little curious about the colorful water.

80
00:04:43.302 --> 00:04:47.124
"You should be able to tell if it's regular water by the taste."

81
00:04:48.628 --> 00:04:49.529
"I'm not tasting that!"

82
00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:51.430
Vilkor looked alarmed.

83
00:04:52.011 --> 00:04:54.732
"What if it's poisoned or enchanted with evil spells?"

84
00:04:55.533 --> 00:04:56.674
Zira stepped forward.

85
00:04:56.694 --> 00:04:57.875
"I'll taste it."

86
00:04:58.535 --> 00:05:03.839
She snatched the pottery cup from Vilkor's hand and then dipped it into the overflowing well.

87
00:05:04.519 --> 00:05:06.140
She lifted the cup toward her lips.

88
00:05:06.761 --> 00:05:10.624
Before she was able to take a sip, the cup cracked down the side.

89
00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:14.726
"Oh, dear," Vilkor said as the water dribbled onto the ground.

90
00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:16.628
Zira frowned.

91
00:05:17.196 --> 00:05:19.457
"Perhaps you were right after all, Vilkor."

92
00:05:20.058 --> 00:05:21.338
She tossed the cup away.

93
00:05:21.358 --> 00:05:25.300
"There's something very wrong with this water.

94
00:05:25.841 --> 00:05:27.622
Perhaps dangerously so."

95
00:05:28.822 --> 00:05:31.084
Perda stared at the cracked cup on the ground.

96
00:05:32.084 --> 00:05:36.727
For some reason it looked vaguely familiar, but she didn't spend much time thinking about that.

97
00:05:37.347 --> 00:05:39.128
She was focused on Zira.

98
00:05:40.048 --> 00:05:45.852
"Am I imagining things," she thought, or had the woman squeezed the cup with her hand to make

99
00:05:45.892 --> 00:05:46.372
it crack?

100
00:05:47.836 --> 00:05:50.779
"What good is a well if you can't drink the water?"

101
00:05:51.119 --> 00:05:52.040
Vilkor complained.

102
00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:56.263
He glared at Mellis as if he blamed her for the whole situation.

103
00:05:57.224 --> 00:05:58.365
Zann rolled his eyes.

104
00:05:58.385 --> 00:06:01.928
"He still doesn't get it," he whispered to Perda.

105
00:06:02.329 --> 00:06:05.051
Before Perda could answer, Zira spoke again.

106
00:06:05.071 --> 00:06:08.754
"Never mind that, my friend," she said to Vilkor.

107
00:06:08.774 --> 00:06:10.776
"We'll get to the bottom of it.

108
00:06:11.752 --> 00:06:17.915
In the meantime we should post guards immediately to keep everyone else away until we figure out what's—"

109
00:06:19.256 --> 00:06:23.818
She was interrupted by a wild howl that sent chills down Perda's spine.

110
00:06:24.598 --> 00:06:30.802
A moment later a creature Perda had never seen before stepped into view from behind a shrub.

111
00:06:31.402 --> 00:06:35.324
It was the size of a small human, covered in rough brown fur.

112
00:06:36.132 --> 00:06:41.334
Sharp, crooked teeth stuck out of a wide mouth that was dripping with slime.

113
00:06:42.254 --> 00:06:48.577
The creature walked on four legs, though its crooked hind legs were much shorter than its forelegs, which

114
00:06:48.697 --> 00:06:51.358
barely touched the ground as it lurched along.

115
00:06:52.338 --> 00:06:54.038
Mellis gasped in terror.

116
00:06:54.058 --> 00:06:55.219
"Oh, no!"

117
00:06:55.659 --> 00:06:56.139
she cried.
